-// Chapter 34 Starter GPU particle lab.
+// Chapter 34 checkpoint 1: establish the GPU particle state and the reset pass.
 //
-// The Starter is an honest deterministic baseline, not a pretend GPU pipeline. The CPU reference advances the
-// particle system, compacts the live set, and the host uploads that compacted state for a direct instanced draw.
-// There is no emission, simulation, compaction, or indirect-argument compute here: the render pass simply draws
-// the particles the reference produced, so the picture on screen is real GPU output while every decision it
-// depends on is made by the auditable CPU contract. The Solution replaces the upload with the equivalent on-GPU
-// passes, and shares this exact draw so the two images agree.
+// The lab stops uploading a CPU reference and starts owning its state on the GPU. This file declares the particle
+// ABI, the unordered-access views the compute passes write, the constant block the host fills every dispatch, and
+// the first pass the frame runs: InitCS clears both state slots to dead particles, zeroes the counters, and seeds
+// the compacted lists and their out-of-bounds sentinels. Emission, simulation, compaction, indirect arguments and
+// the checksum arrive in later checkpoints; their bindings are declared here so the resource layout is stable, but
+// nothing writes them yet.
+
+#define LGP_PARTICLE_THREAD_GROUP_SIZE 256
 
